          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"category\":\"widespread_digitizer_feature_anomaly\",\"cause\":\"unknown; a common-mode digitizer/readout or AutoDQM reference/normalization problem is more plausible than a localized PMT, LVDS, or trigger-rate fault\",\"action\":\"First verify subrun exposure normalization and inspect raw waveforms plus per-subrun pulse-count, pulse-height, and pulse-area distributions for representative flagged and unflagged channels. Compare digitizer configuration and software/reference versions with a known-good run, and obtain board-matching, synchronization, queue-occupancy, CPU, and digitizer-rate telemetry. If raw data confirm a common digitizer/readout failure, restart or resynchronize the affected DAQ component; if raw data are normal, correct the AutoDQM baseline or zero-variance z-score handling instead.\",\"confidence\":0.35,\"supporting_historical_runs\":[1500,1605,2126],\"reasoning_summary\":\"OBSERVED: all 129 subruns are anomalous, with 10,816 channel-entries and several channels showing extreme pulse-feature z-scores. The recorded trigger rate remains stable near 4.857 Hz, and LVDS has no persistent zero, missing, high, or low signal pin. No missing detector channels are reported. INFERRED: the breadth and persistence favor a common-mode data-processing, digitizer, or DAQ-readout issue; they contradict the localized signatures of broken PMT bases and the elevated-rate signatures of LVDS noise. The final count transitions may reflect reduced exposure because rates remain stable. No exact historical match exists: runs 1605 and 2126 partially share million-scale nPulses anomalies on channels 47/69 or 50/69, while run 1500 was anomalous throughout, but their confirmed diagnoses are inconsistent or incomplete. UNKNOWN: raw waveform behavior, exposure normalization, board matching, queue state, synchronization, CPU load, digitizer rates, and within-run configuration. These checks discriminate a real common-mode readout fault from an AutoDQM baseline artifact.\"}"
        }
      ],
